[144.457128, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m5\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[144.457813, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe failure comes from GCC tokenizing the literal `\"\"\"` even inside a skipped conditional. I’ll test which multiline Python string delimiter GCC tolerates in a \r\nskipped group, then apply the successful form.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncat > /tmp/t1.c <<'EOF'\r\n#if 0\r\n\"\"\"\r\n#endif\r\n#include <stdio.h>\r\nint main(void){puts(\"C1\");return 0;}\r\n#if 0\r\n\"\"\"\r\n#endif\r\nimport sys\r\nprint(\"PY\")\r\nEOF\r\ncat > /tmp/t2.c <<'EOF'\r\n#if 0\r\n'''\r\n#endif\r\n#include <stdio.h>\r\nint main(void){puts(\"C2\");return 0;}\r\n#if 0\r\n'''\r\n#endif\r\nimport sys\r\nprint(\"PY\")\r\nEOF\r\nfor f in /tmp/t1.c /tmp/t2.c; do echo \"=== $f gcc ===\"; gcc -std=c11 -w \"$f\" -o /tmp/t.out 2>&1 && /tmp/t.out; echo \"=== $f python ===\"; python3 \"$f\" 2>&1; done\r\n```\r\n"]
[144.457829, "o", "\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[144.458119, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[144.50228, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[144.502919, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n=== /tmp/t1.c gcc ===\r\n/tmp/t1.c:9:1: error: unknown type name ‘import’\r\n    9 | import sys\r\n      | ^~~~~~\r\n/tmp/t1.c:10:1: error: expected ‘=’, ‘,’, ‘;’, ‘asm’ or ‘__attribute__’ before ‘print’\r\n   10 | print(\"PY\")\r\n      | ^~~~~\r\n=== /tmp/t1.c python ===\r\nPY\r\n=== /tmp/t2.c gcc ===\r\n/tmp/t2.c:9:1: error: unknown type name ‘import’\r\n    9 | import sys\r\n      | ^~~~~~\r\n/tmp/t2.c:10:1: error: expected ‘=’, ‘,’, ‘;’, ‘asm’ or ‘__attribute__’ before ‘print’\r\n   10 | print(\"PY\")\r\n      | ^~~~~\r\n=== /tmp/t2.c python ===\r\nPY\r\n\r\n"]
