[195.960983, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m11\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[195.961885, "o", "\r\u001b[2KI found the actual structural issue: the second `#endif` closes the guard before the Python code, so GCC still sees Python. The fix is to add a third `#if \r\n0`/`#endif` pair around the Python-only section; Python treats those as comments, while C skips the section entirely.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncat > /tmp/t7.c <<'EOF'\r\n#if 0\r\n\"\"\"\"\r\n#endif\r\n#include <stdio.h>\r\nint main(void){puts(\"C7\");return 0;}\r\n#if 0\r\n\"\"\"\"\" # \"\r\n#endif\r\n#if 0\r\nimport sys\r\nprint(\"PY\")\r\n#endif\r\nEOF\r\necho '--- gcc ---'; gcc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra /tmp/t7.c -o /tmp/t7.out 2>&1 && /tmp/t7.out\r\necho '--- python ---'; python3 /tmp/t7.c 2>&1\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[195.962064, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[196.009759, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n--- gcc ---\r\nC7\r\n--- python ---\r\nPY\r\n\r\n"]
[196.010922, "o", "\u001b[92m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[?25l"]
