[214.205425, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe file now compiles cleanly and passes Python bytecode compilation. I’ll run the exact commands requested and compare both implementations over edge cases and\r\nlarger indices.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\ngcc /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /app/polyglot/cmain\r\nfor n in 0 1 2 3 4 5 10 20 50 90 92 93 100 500 1000 5000 10000; do\r\n  py=$(python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c \"$n\")\r\n  c=$(/app/polyglot/cmain \"$n\")\r\n  if [ \"$py\" != \"$c\" ]; then\r\n    echo \"MISMATCH n=$n\"; echo \"python=$py\"; echo \"c=$c\"; exit 1\r\n  fi\r\ndone\r\necho \"SAMPLES_MATCH\"\r\nfor n in $(seq 0 300); do\r\n  chk=$(/app/polyglot/cmain \"$n\")\r\n  expected=$(python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c \"$n\")\r\n  [ \"$chk\" = \"$expected\" ] || { echo \"MISMATCH at $n\"; exit 1; }\r\ndone\r\necho \"RANGE_0_300_MATCH\"\r\necho \"PWD=$(pwd)\"\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
