[317.98171, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m20\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[317.982574, "o", "\r\u001b[2KBoth versions now agree at 100,000 and the exact requested commands print the expected result. I’ll do a final clean compile/check, including `-Werror`, and \r\nremove test artifacts so the deliverable is only the requested source file.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\n# Final broad correctness check while build artifacts are still available.\r\nfor n in $(seq 0 1000); do\r\n  [ \"$(python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c \"$n\")\" = \"$(/app/polyglot/cmain \"$n\")\" ] || { echo \"MISMATCH at $n\"; exit 1; }\r\ndone\r\necho \"FINAL_RANGE_0_1000_MATCH\"\r\n# Ensure a strict build remains warning-free.\r\ngcc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror -O2 /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /tmp/cmain_strict\r\n[ \"$(python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 250)\" = \"$(/tmp/cmain_strict 250)\" ]\r\necho \"STRICT_BUILD_OK\"\r\n# Keep only the requested single source file.\r\nrm -f /app/polyglot/cmain\r\nrm -rf /app/polyglot/__pycache__\r\nfind /app/polyglot -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -printf '%f\\n' | sort\r\npython3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 20\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[317.983699, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[328.505003, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
